    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Google</span><span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Dropbox</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Pattern: Handling Large Blobs</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Videos, photos, backups, attachments, model weights: big binary files break designs built for small JSON. After this page you can explain why bytes should never pass through your API servers, how presigned multipart uploads survive a dropped connection at 99%, how to keep the database and the blob store in agreement, and how downloads get fast and safe.</p>\n      "
